      "narrative": "Mara's cup pauses halfway to her lips. She sets it down with a soft click.\n\n\"Toran Vex,\" she says, nodding toward the bar. \"He's the lockwright. Sworn to the Kestrel Guild. Kept the Ash Gate's mechanism oiled and true for years.\"\n\nToran flinches at his name, shoulders hunching. He busies himself wiping a glass that's already clean.\n\n\"But I already told you\u2014the Guild sealed it after Old Bram died. Toran doesn't work that lock anymore. None of us go near the Gate.\"\n\nShe says it flatly. Final. But her thumb traces the rim of her cup in a slow, deliberate circle\u2014a nervous tell she's trying to hide.\n\nYou caught the name. You got the answer. But there's something beneath it\u2014a current she's steering you away from. The way she emphasized *after Old Bram died* felt pointed, like she's feeding you a scripted line. And Toran's silence at the bar is louder than any denial."
    },
