      "narrative": "The question hangs in the air between you. Mara's thumb stops its circling on the cup's rim.\n\nFor a long moment, she doesn't speak. When she does, her voice is quieter.\n\n\"Old Bram,\" she says. \"He was the ferryman. He worked the lock. He took the coin and ran the line.\"\n\nShe meets your eyes, and there's something raw there now\u2014a crack in that rehearsed composure. \"He'd take people through the Grey for a price. Had his own rates, his own schedule, his own... rules. The Guild turned a blind eye because he paid his tithe and kept the mechanism clean.\"\n\nToran Vex has stopped pretending to wipe the glass. He's watching the two of you now, a sheen of sweat on his brow.\n\n\"But that's all dead now,\" Mara finishes. \"Gate's sealed. Bram's gone. Whatever he knew, whatever he carried, it went into the ground with him.\"\n\nShe gives you the name. She gives you the role. But the way her jaw tightens on *into the ground with him*\u2014there's a name she's *not* saying. Someone else who knew the route. Someone still breathing.\n\nThe tavern creaks in the rain. Mara watches you, waiting to see if you push further."
    },
