      "narrative": "Your voice carries into the mist\u2014\"Old Bram!\"\u2014and the sound is swallowed, absorbed by the fog like a stone dropped into deep water. No echo. No rebound off the arch's stone. Just silence rushing in to fill the space where your voice was.\n\nThe mist beyond the Gate stirs, curls shifting in some current you can't feel on this side. For a moment, the grey seems to thicken, to press against the invisible barrier of the arch. Then it settles again, indifferent.\n\nNo answer comes. Not a footstep, not a whisper, not the creak of a mechanism long seized.\n\nThe copper coin lies in the gravel at your feet, catching the dull morning light. The filed lock housing stares back at you, a blind socket where iron was shaved smooth.\n\nWhoever Old Bram was, whatever he carried\u2014the Gate isn't giving it up."
